PVD("afghanistan_ndp_2021-2025",{"docs":["","AFG ANPDF 2021 2025"],"s":{"1":[[1,"43","6","Urban Development Program","The current Urban Development Program aims to strengthen urban governance, improve urban economies, environment, housing, infrastructure and public transport (A-SDG, 1-2-11), strengthen urban-rural linkages, provide housing and reintegration facilities to returnees, facilitate kuchis' habitation in accordance with the provision of article 14 of the constitution, and ensure balanced growth and urban population decentralization.",""],[1,"44","1","Urban Development Program Reprioritization","We will reprioritize urban development programs within the larger framework of regional development (geographical zones) for the years 2021-25.",""],[1,"44","1","Urban National Priority Program Implementation","The Urban NPP was approved by the Urban High Council in July 2016 with the aim of making cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient, and sustainable.",""],[1,"44","1","Urban Vision Implementation","We must now move towards the implementation of our vision.",""],[1,"44","1","Urban City Development Blueprint Preparation","We engaged the world-class Boston-based firm Sasaki, and developed the blueprints for the development of our cities over the past five years.",""]],"2":[[1,"35","2","State-Building National Priority Programmes","Through state- building NPPs, our objects are to combat corruption, strengthen sub-national governance, improve infrastructures, build human capital and improve public financial management systems.",""],[1,"37","3","Effective Governance Program","We will continue to be responsive to the demands of citizens and strengthen the accountability and transparency of the institutions, and implement further actions to address governance and the rule of law, in particular, towards curbing corruption and encouraging private investment by reducing the perceptions of high risk and low returns on capital.",""],[1,"38","1","Civil Service Biometric and Biographical Data Completion","Completion of the biometric and biographical data of the civil service - already 90 percent completed-in the coming months will provide a reliable information base for comprehensive reform and significant savings in the recurrent budget.",""],[1,"39","3","Government Implementation Capacity Strengthening Program","With this new program, Afghanistan will increase capacity in many support areas, including auditing, finance, and procurement.",""],[1,"39","3","Targeted Certification Training Program","We will create targeted training programs for certifications in critical areas (ensuring gender parity in terms of access to training programs), create regulations to set standards and create a framework for output indicators for each ministry.",""],[1,"39","3","Standards and Output Indicator Framework","We will create regulations to set standards and create a framework for output indicators for each ministry.",""],[1,"49","2","Government Accountability for Service Delivery","Hold the government accountable to implement its part of the deal in providing services to Afghans.",""],[1,"49","9","Procurement Reform Expansion to Line Ministries","Expand procurement reforms to line ministries to cover contract management.",""],[1,"52","7","Institutional and Governance Strengthening","The current political institutions and economic and governance structures will be maintained and strengthened.",""],[1,"58","11","Project Implementation Capacity Strengthening","SO 8.1: Promote efficient and effective implementation of projects by increasing capacity in planning, implementation, auditing, finance, and procurement.",""],[1,"60","1","Public Sector Governance Improvement","IR 5.1.2: Improve governance in public sector management.",""],[1,"60","1","Professional Civil Service Reform","IR 5.1.4: Establish a professional civil service through systematic training and capacity building programs and transparent recruitment procedures.",""]],"3":[[1,"44","3","Counter-Narcotics and Anti-Money Laundering Measures","To ensure effective counternarcotic and anti-money laundering measures and legal, transparent and sustainable exploitation and management of mineral resources, the government plans the following:",""],[1,"45","2","Regional Cooperation Against Illicit Trade and Resource Trafficking","Cooperating in a shared responsibility with our neighboring countries to combat and prevent illicit trade, trafficking and illegal exploitation of natural resources.",""],[1,"45","3","Commodity Monitoring and Certification Scheme Improvement","Ensuring effective national security and improving custom structures - 'improving commodity monitoring and certification schemes.'",""],[1,"45","4","Cross-Border Communication and Cooperation Mechanisms","Creating effective cross border communication and cooperation mechanisms at all important border crossing points - Torkham, Chaman, Gulam Khan and Nawa Pass (Pakistan); Islam Quala and Zaranj (Islamic Republic of Iran); Hayraton (Uzbekistan); Toraghundi and Aquina (Turkmenistan); and Shir Khan, Eshkeshem, Shegnan, Nusay, and Al Shanem (Tajikistan).",""],[1,"61","5","Combat Illicit Natural Resource Exploitation and Opium Poppy Trafficking","Combat illicit exploitation of natural resources and the cultivation, production and trafficking of opium poppy.",""]],"4":[[1,"5","2","Strengthen Institutions and Services for Lasting Peace","solidify and strengthen the institutions and services required to secure and sustain a lasting peace",""],[1,"5","6","Peace-Building, State-Building, and Market-Building Strategy","ANPDF II is focused on three broad objectives: peace-building, state-building, and market- building.",""],[1,"5","6","National Priority Programs Alignment with Afghanistan SDGs","we elaborate on our strategies and implementation plans, including our national priority programs, which are aligned with Afghanistan Sustainable Development Goals (henceforth A-SDGs).",""],[1,"6","3","Core State Functions Reform","Core state functions will be reformed systematically to ensure that the government's approaches can be fully implemented.",""],[1,"45","8","Country-Led National Development Framework","As we consider the next five years, the Afghan government and Afghan people look forward to developing and delivering on a single, country-led framework, together with donors and international partners.",""],[1,"49","3","Mutual Accountability Reform Incentives","Incentivize mutual accountability reforms through the ARTF Incentive DPG and the EU SRBC.",""]],"5":[[1,"59","1","International Partnership Expansion for Trade, Transit, Investment, Guarantees, and Digital Knowledge Networks","SO 11: Expand the tools of international partnership from Aid to trade, transit, investment, guarantees, and digital networks of knowledge.",""],[1,"60","2","Afghanistan Participation in Global Governance","IR 5.1.5: Promote Afghanistan's participation in global governance.",""],[1,"61","1","Regional Integration Programs for Economic Cooperation","Transform the emerging consensus on regional connectivity into focused programs of regional integration for economic cooperation.",""]],"6":[[1,"48","3","Public and Private Sector Systems and Leadership Capacity Building","We, therefore, propose that our partners work with us on a set of policy conditions in return for on-budget support to enable us to focus national energies on building systems and programs, and cultivating leaderships and management skills, in the government and the private sector.",""]],"7":[[1,"6","3","Court Reform and Constitutional Rights Enforcement","we will step up the fight against corruption, reform our courts, and make sure that ordinary citizens can exert their constitutional rights with confidence.",""]],"8":[[1,"41","3","Business Enabling Environment Reform","we reaffirm our commitment to improving the business enabling environment (Doing Business reforms), establishing instruments for risk sharing, and jointly with the business community, identifying opportunities for improving security for the sector.",""],[1,"41","3","SME Risk Management Support","We will ensure that existing businesses, especially SMEs, are better equipped to manage the risks and uncertainties presented by Afghanistan's country context.",""],[1,"41","3","Women-Led Business Access Reform","This will involve removing barriers to the participation of women in the economy and that all services are accessible to businesses led and organized by women.",""],[1,"41","3","Access to Finance and Production Inputs Facilitation","We will focus on increasing access to finance, promoting financial inclusion and improving, facilitating and streamlining procedure to enhance access to production inputs, including access to land, labor, and electricity at reasonable prices.",""],[1,"41","4","Business Service Outreach and Line Ministry Capacity Strengthening","We will engage in greater outreach and increase the capacity of line ministries and agencies to better serve and deliver essential services to the business community and resolve issues in a coordinated and structured fashion.","line ministries and agencies"],[1,"61","9","Commercial Law Reform for Private Sector Growth","IR 13.5: Develop commercial laws that stimulate and support private sector growth.",""],[1,"61","9","Formalization of Informal Businesses","IR 13.6: Increase revenue coming from the sector by reducing the number of businesses operating as informal.",""],[1,"61","9","Enabling Environment for Knowledge-Based Enterprise Creation","IR 13.7: Ensure an enabling legal and political environment that encourages practical application of know-how in the creation of new economic enterprises.",""],[1,"65","1","Commercial Law Reform for Private Sector Growth","IO 13.1: commercial laws that support private sector growth promoted.",""],[1,"65","2","Private Enterprise Licensing and Registration Streamlining","IO 13.2: licensing and registration requirements for private enterprises streamlined.",""]],"9":[[1,"6","4","Market-Building Economic Development Programs","We will do this by creating and implementing programs for poverty eradication and economic development through the lens of market-building, based on Afghanistan's eight sources of capital, as well as our comparative and competitive advantages.",""],[1,"13","2","National Infrastructure Implementation Company","Thanks to the formation of a national implementation company that works closely with small and medium construction companies.",""],[1,"26","2","Labor-Intensive Small-Scale Industrial Unit Establishment","In the short-term, the establishment of labor-intensive small-scale industrial units",""],[1,"26","2","Manufacturing Sector Diversification Initiative","in the medium term, diversification away from agriculture to the manufacturing sector is essential",""],[1,"28","2","Labor-Intensive Economic Stimulus Program","This program aims to increase economic activity and employment by focusing on labor intensive projects that have quick returns, but also long-term growth potential.",""],[1,"43","3","Small-Scale Labor-Intensive Industrialization and Domestic Market Development","The government will also focus on small-scale labor intensive industrialization and creating domestic markets that will have a large capacity to localize certain products in which Afghanistan has competitive and productive advantage, thereby reducing the deficit in trade, creating employment, and ultimately reducing poverty.",""],[1,"43","3","Three-Phase Industrial Development Framework","Based on this strategy, we are taking a three-phased framework approach: (1) primary goods development, (2) light industrial development, and (3) heavy industrial development",""],[1,"43","4","Light Industry Development Reform","The second stage of reforms would include the development of light industries, thus generating higher levels of employment and reducing poverty.",""],[1,"43","4","Heavy Industry Development Reform","Afghanistan is already working on both light and heavy industrial development.",""],[1,"43","5","Industrial Policy Development Support","International support for the development of our industrial base could include support for policy development, as well as support for the development of physical infrastructures such as industrial parks, power generation and transmission for industries, skills development for manufacturing and industry, and simplification of the land allocation process.",""],[1,"43","5","Industrial Infrastructure Development","International support for the development of our industrial base could include support for policy development, as well as support for the development of physical infrastructures such as industrial parks, power generation and transmission for industries, skills development for manufacturing and industry, and simplification of the land allocation process.",""],[1,"43","5","Manufacturing and Industry Skills Development","International support for the development of our industrial base could include support for policy development, as well as support for the development of physical infrastructures such as industrial parks, power generation and transmission for industries, skills development for manufacturing and industry, and simplification of the land allocation process.",""],[1,"43","5","Land Allocation Process Simplification","International support for the development of our industrial base could include support for policy development, as well as support for the development of physical infrastructures such as industrial parks, power generation and transmission for industries, skills development for manufacturing and industry, and simplification of the land allocation process.",""],[1,"61","4","Productivity and Market Access Support for Competitive Advantage Sectors","Increase labor and capital productivity in areas that Afghanistan has competitive advantage (e.g. dried fruits and nuts, marble, a route for energy transit, gems, rare earth minerals and lithium), by enhancing skills and facilitating access to wider markets.",""],[1,"61","10","Construction and Building Materials Industry Strengthening","IR 14.1.5: Strengthen local and national construction and building materials industry.",""]],"10":[[1,"25","4","Primary Sector Development Programme","adopts primary sector development (agriculture and mining)",""],[1,"42","4","Mining Sector Reform for Transparency and Sustainable Extraction","In the short term, the mining sector will continue to implement reforms to improve transparency and sustainable extraction.",""],[1,"42","4","Mining Sector Reform Strategy for Sustainable Resource Development","The current reform strategy aims to ensure Afghanistan's natural resources are sustainably developed, compliant with the Extractive Industries Transparency Initiative (EITI), and public revenues are fully collected.",""],[1,"42","4","Ministry of Mines and Petroleum Capacity Support","The program aims to ensure that the Ministry of Mines and Petroleum can fulfill its","Ministry of Mines and Petroleum"],[1,"43","1","Mining Sector National Priority Programme","The Mining Sector NPP focuses on five key areas in order to improve the performance of Afghanistan's minerals and hydrocarbons sectors: (1) Institutional Reform and Development, (2) Geological Data Acquisition and Management, (3) Contract Management and Compliance, (4) Transparent and Accountable Governance, and (5) Growth and Enabling Environment.",""],[1,"59","3","Knowledge-Based Extractives Sector Development","SO 12.3: Develop a knowledge-based, sustainable, transparent, and efficient extractives sector that supports Afghanistan's broad-based and inclusive development.",""]],"11":[[1,"40","6","Predictable Investment Regulatory Framework","Ensure good regulatory design and maintain a predictable regulatory framework for investment.",""],[1,"40","7","Private Sector Participation in Infrastructure Development","Encourage private sector's participation in infrastructure development.",""],[1,"40","13","Market-Building and Competitive Strategy Development","Our market-building programs will bank on Afghanistan's natural, man-made, financial, institutional, knowledge, human, cultural, and political capitals.",""],[1,"41","4","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Development","We will present opportunities for public private partnerships (PPP) in order to develop infrastructure that facilitates a business-enabling environment, enhances connectivity, and scales investment.",""],[1,"47","2","Guarantee Support for Investment and Regional Connectivity","Guarantees can play a crucial function in enabling foreign direct investment, repatriation of Afghan capital from the region, assumption of risks by farmers, entrepreneurs, industrialists, and mining and oil and gas companies.",""],[1,"47","2","Risk Guarantees for Large-Scale Regional Connectivity Programs","Guarantees against different forms of risks can be also be crucial in the design and implementation of large- scale programs of regional connectivity, ranging from gas pipelines to transmission lines and transport systems.",""],[1,"48","4","National Public-Private Partnership Delivery Mechanism","Focus on NPPs as the preferred mechanism of delivery of state functions allows us to explore outcome base criteria for development projects.",""],[1,"48","4","Outcome-Based Project Delivery Standards","Agreement on quality standards and delivery timelines rather than project-by-project management could enhance efficiency and allow Afghanistan's competitive capacity in the construction sector, along the lines of Ethiopia and Rwanda, among others.",""],[1,"60","7","Public-Private Partnership and Private Investment Promotion in Infrastructure","IR 9.5: Increase public-private partnerships (PPPs) and encourage private sector investment in infrastructure development.",""]],"12":[[1,"42","3","Agriculture NPP Refresh and Implementation","The Agriculture NPP was designed to meet these objectives and was approved by the Cabinet in 2016 and is currently being refreshed to meet pressing needs.",""],[1,"59","3","Sustainable Agriculture Development Initiatives","SO 12.1: Promote sustainable agriculture by developing new initiatives designed to stimulate the growth of existing and new agricultural products for domestic consumption and exports.",""],[1,"59","3","Agricultural Production and Productivity Management Strengthening","SO 12.2: Promote and strengthen effective management of agricultural production and productivity to ensure national food and nutrition security and increased household incomes.",""],[1,"61","4","Agricultural Productivity and Food Production Enhancement","Eliminate hunger by improving agriculture productivity and increasing food production.",""]],"13":[[1,"24","3","Agricultural Productivity Investment Package","We also will ramp up investments in water management, seeds, and other livestock practices to raise agricultural productivity.",""],[1,"25","5","Agriculture, Irrigation, and Related Infrastructure Acceleration Program","the government considers accelerating the development of agriculture, irrigation and related infrastructures as its top national priority program.",""],[1,"26","6","Agriculture, Irrigation, and Livestock Development Programme","Accelerating the development of agriculture, irrigation, and livestock, which will generate higher incomes in rural areas (including those which have borne the brunt of conflict), substitute for imports, reduce poverty, and create jobs.",""],[1,"28","2","Watershed and Waterway Management Infrastructure","Projects aiding the management of Watershed and Waterways include the construction of 1,500 small scale check dams to increase agricultural productivity, mitigate flood and drought risk in upper catchments, and prevent sediment transport and soil erosion.",""],[1,"28","2","New Irrigation Canal Construction","This includes the construction of new irrigation canals from established water sources to expand the amount of arable land in the country.",""],[1,"61","4","Farmer Access to Land, Water, and Improved Seeds","Ensure improved access of farmers to land, water, and reformed seeds.",""]],"14":[[1,"29","5","Climate-Resilient Livelihood and Agricultural Practices Initiative","In cooperation with the civil society organizations, the government takes the initiatives to promote climate-resilient livelihood strategies and agricultural practices, public awareness of the impacts of climate change, effective and timely responses to the vulnerabilities of critical sectors, adaptive and integrated land and water management as its top environmental and climate change priorities.",""],[1,"42","3","Famine Action Mechanism","In addition, a Famine Action Mechanism to address water scarcity, food security, and famine risk in Afghanistan was established in 2019.",""],[1,"42","3","Dryland Farming Policy","Several other policies and laws have been amended or approved, including the Dryland Farming Policy, a flagship initiative that will support poverty reduction through climate-smart improvements in subsistence agriculture.",""]],"15":[[1,"21","13","Agriculture and Mineral Sector Reform Programme","Refresh overall strategy and continue to develop the program.",""]],"16":[[1,"28","2","Agricultural Cold Storage and Processing Facilities","For the Agricultural Sector, the program targets the construction of zero-energy cold-storage, drying facilities, and value-added processing plants to both build potential export markets and extend the life of crops to aid food security.",""],[1,"42","3","Agribusiness Charter Operationalization","The Agribusiness Charter, launched in 2018, was the first subprogram in the 2016 Agriculture NPP and is currently being operationalized.",""],[1,"43","4","Domestic Value Addition for Primary Goods","First, we will invest more in developing our primary goods-namely, agricultural and mineral resources - within the country before export.",""],[1,"61","4","Agri-processing Capacity Development for Agricultural Exports","Increase agriculture exports by supporting the development of Agri-processing capacity.",""]],"17":[[1,"24","4","Revision of the National Infrastructure Plan","We will also revise the National Infrastructure plan to accelerate access to reliable electric power and internet, and meet the urgent needs of the private sector for investment and expansion and a program to enhance access through technology by distance learning.",""],[1,"24","11","Revised National Infrastructure Program","A revised National Infrastructure Program to accelerate access to reliable electric power and the internet, and meet the urgent needs of the private sector for investment and expansion.",""],[1,"26","9","Targeted Energy, Mineral, and Regional Integration Investment Acceleration","Accelerating targeted energy, mineral, and regional integration investments that can yield",""],[1,"28","2","Electricity Grid Expansion","Finally, the stimulus plan aims to lay the foundations for future growth by expanding the electricity grid to increase coverage from 40 percent to 60 percent of the population.",""],[1,"51","4","Hydropower Generation and Transmission Infrastructure Investment","World Bank's modeling shows that, by prioritizing investment in hydro generation and important transmission infrastructure, 'Afghanistan could generate in excess of 5 TWh of electricity for export beginning",""]],"18":[[1,"25","1","Enhanced Regional Connectivity for Railways and Transmission Lines","An Enhanced Regional Connectivity to accelerate existing projects and expand those railways and transmission lines essential to relief and recovery.",""],[1,"28","2","Cobble Stone Skills and Rural Access Program","Connectivity initiatives involve both Cobble Stone programs to build skills in rural youth and improve access in remote communities, construction of critical rural roads and national highway maintenance programs.",""],[1,"28","2","Rural Roads and Highway Maintenance Program","Connectivity initiatives involve both Cobble Stone programs to build skills in rural youth and improve access in remote communities, construction of critical rural roads and national highway maintenance programs.",""],[1,"64","3","Railway Extension from Customs Points Inland","Prioritized the extension of railways from custom points inland.",""]],"19":[[1,"60","5","University Teacher Scholarship and Capacity Development","IR 6.7: Improve faculty and staff's capacity by securing scholarship and higher education opportunities within the country for university teachers.",""]],"20":[[1,"24","10","National Human Capital Program for Distance Learning Access","A National Human Capital Program to enhance access through technology to distance learning through reprogramming of existing projects into a program.",""],[1,"38","3","National Technical and Vocational Education and Training Strategy","The TVET strategy is developed for improving equitable access to technical and vocational education, strengthening quality assurance and relevancy of TVET and reforming the TVET management system.",""],[1,"60","5","Higher Education and TVET Access Expansion","IR 6.6: Improve access to Higher Education and Technical and Vocational Education and Training (TVET).",""]],"21":[[1,"11","5","Policy for Improving Girls' Education","The GoIRA approved a Policy for Improving Girl's Education that provides required guidelines and mandates policy initiatives to enhance girls'",""],[1,"60","5","School Enrollment and Teacher Professional Development","IR 6.1: Increase school enrollments and improve the professional skills of teachers.",""],[1,"60","5","Pre-School Education Expansion in Disadvantaged and Remote Areas","IR 6.2: Provide quality and balanced pre-school education services for all girls and boys, especially in disadvantaged and remote areas.",""],[1,"60","5","School Enrollment and Adult Literacy Improvement","IR 6.3: Improve school enrollment rate and adult literacy rate with increasing attention on improving girl's education.",""],[1,"60","5","Inclusive Education for Children with Special Needs and Returnees","IR 6.4: Ensure inclusion of children with special needs and the children of returnees and IDPs.",""],[1,"60","5","Islamic School Reorganization for Enrollment Expansion","IR 6.5: Reorganize Islamic education schools to increase student enrollment in areas with low public education enrollment.",""],[1,"63","10","National Madrasa Registration and Curriculum Development","IO 6.4: Register all MADRASAs across the country with the Ministry of Education, and develop and distribute their curriculum.","Ministry of Education"],[1,"63","12","Adult Literacy Training with Material Incentives","Provide literacy-training opportunities accompanied by material incentives to # adult men and women across the country by 2025.",""],[1,"63","14","Teacher Training Policy Finalization and Teacher Recruitment","Finalize the teacher training policy, and recruit 65000 qualified teachers across the country equitably and transparently.",""],[1,"63","16","School Textbook Update and Distribution under New Curriculum Framework","Update, publish and distribute ## school textbooks based on the new curriculum framework by 2025.",""],[1,"63","17","Distance Education Regulation","Approved the regulation of distance education",""],[1,"63","17","Private Sector Curriculum Publishing Authorization","Approved the regulation of granting the right to the private sector for publishing school's curriculum",""],[1,"63","17","Private Schools Activities Regulation Amendment","Amended the regulation of private schools activities",""]],"22":[[1,"21","5","Integrated Education and Health Delivery Programs","Combine education and health delivery programs",""],[1,"27","4","Expansion of Reproductive and Other Health Services","We will continue to expand access to reproductive and other health services",""]],"23":[[1,"60","8","Nutrition and Family Planning Improvement Program","IR 10.1: Improve children's and women's nutrition status and increase utilization and coverage of family planning methods.",""],[1,"60","8","Polio and Tuberculosis Eradication Program","IR 10.2: Design and implement effective program aimed at eradicating polio and tuberculosis (TB).",""],[1,"60","8","Polio Vaccination Access Expansion","IR 10.3: Reduce accessibility challenges to polio vaccination.",""],[1,"60","8","Outreach for Chronically Missed Children in Inaccessible Areas","IR 10.4: Cover the chronically missed children in inaccessible areas.",""],[1,"60","8","Women's Reproductive Health Access Expansion","IR 10.5: Increase women's access to reproductive health services.",""],[1,"64","2","Routine Immunization Coverage Improvement","High routine immunization coverage provided, (2) improved management quality to increase the quality campaigns, (3) enhanced effective communication to reduce large-scale vaccination refusal rates.",""]],"24":[[1,"38","2","Education Program Revision for Distance Learning Access","To respond to COVID-19, we will revise education programs to also enhance access through technology to distance learning.",""],[1,"38","2","National Health Program Preparedness and Capacity Revision","We are also revising the national health program to increase health sector preparedness and capacity.",""],[1,"53","1","National Priority Program Sequencing Under Base Case Scenario","Therefore, we plan, design, and sequence our National Priority Programs as per the assumptions outlined in our base case scenario.",""]],"25":[[1,"18","3","Reconfiguration of National Assistance Programs","Existing national programs are being reconfigured to provide more direct forms of assistance to the poor, with particular attention to the ultra-poor.",""],[1,"24","7","National Human Security Program","A National Human Security Program, involving the expansion of the Citizen Charter program and restructuring of higher UN-run Humanitarian fund, to assist groups facing structural risk.",""],[1,"24","8","National Recovery Program for Threatened Groups","A National Recovery Program to assist groups threatened by situational risk, engaging provincial, municipal, and district authorities and civic organizations and private sector associations.",""],[1,"24","9","National Stimulus Program","A National Stimulus Program, directed to balance social and spatial development.",""],[1,"27","4","Inclusive Social Investment and Safety Net Expansion","The government will continue to invest in education, health care, food and nutrition security and the safety net in a way that increases gender equity and covers all vulnerable populations, including IDPs, Kuchis, people with disability and the heirs of martyrs and the poorest segments of the society",""]],"26":[[1,"24","3","Reintegration Support for Internally Displaced People and Returnees","The government will take measures to re-integrate internally displaced people and returnees from Iran, Pakistan, and elsewhere due to COVID-19.",""],[1,"24","3","Household Resilience Building in Rural Areas","In the longer term, the government will support the Afghan people in becoming more shock-proof by building resilience among poorer households in rural areas.",""]],"27":[[1,"45","6","Alternative Livelihoods and Rural Economic Recovery Programme","Effective counternarcotic policies such as providing alternative livelihoods and focusing efforts on rebuilding the rural economy and creating off-farm opportunities.",""],[1,"59","12","Job Creation Programs for Crime and Violence Reduction","Reduce the level of crimes and violence, by comprehensive planning and financing of job creation programs.",""],[1,"60","6","Social Protection and Labor-Intensive Public Works Initiatives","IR 7.2: Reduce unemployment by directing CCs focus on poverty alleviation initiatives such as social protection projects and other labor- intensive public works programs.",""]],"28":[[1,"60","2","Child Labor Elimination and Child Protection Measures","IR 5.1.6: Eliminate or significantly reduce child labor and end exploitation, torture, sexual abuse and violence against children.",""]],"29":[[1,"44","1","Urban Property Rights Strengthening","Enjoyment of firm property rights by urban Afghans will also be an enduring legacy of this program.",""],[1,"61","10","Affordable and Social Housing Promotion","IR 14.1.1: Promoting new affordable and social housing.",""],[1,"61","10","Informal Settlement Upgrading","IR 14.1.2: Upgrading informal settlements to integrate into the city fabric.",""],[1,"61","10","Urban Renewal in Major Cities","IR 14.1.3: Undertake urban renewal in the five major cities to transform inner-city neighborhoods.",""],[1,"61","10","Neighborhood Public Space and Facility Improvement","IR 14.1.4: Improve neighborhood-level public spaces and facilities.",""],[1,"61","10","Urban Poverty Reduction and Household Resilience","IR 14.2.1: Reduce urban poverty and strenathen the resilience of urban households.",""]],"30":[[1,"13","3","Informal Settlement Property Rights Regularization","Property rights are being affirmed and extended to informal urban settlements.",""],[1,"13","3","Public Asset Inventory and Land Grabbing Reversal","Public assets are being inventoried, and the widespread land grabbing is being systematically reversed.",""],[1,"13","3","Natural Resource Inventories and Databases for Future Generations","Inventories and databases of our pastures, forests, rivers and mountains are being prepared to ensure the rights of future generations.",""]],"31":[[1,"5","6","Development Partnership Framework","Sixth, we provide an overview of the future fiscal scenarios,",""],[1,"7","5","Governance Review of National Programs and Internationally Financed Projects","Optimize programs and partnerships (A-SDG 17): Review of the governance of national programs and internationally-financed projects in terms of accountability, effectiveness, efficiency, equity, transparency, manageability, inclusivity and legitimacy to arrive at a double-compact between the state and citizens, and between the government and international partners.",""],[1,"7","6","Conditions-Based Aid Metrics and Conditionality Framework","Establish metrics for conditions-based aid: Reach an agreement on conditionality with developmental partners that are robust, measurable and manageable in the policy area, and outcome-oriented in terms of programs and projects.",""],[1,"9","5","Mutual Accountability Frameworks for Development Cooperation","We have continued to deliver on our mutual commitments since the 2014 Self- Reliance Mutual Accountability Framework 2014-2018 and the current Geneva Mutual Accountability Framework 2019-2020.",""],[1,"16","2","Budget Support Accountability and Performance Framework","Finally, the ANPDF II provides a framework for our international partners to have confidence that more flexible support to the budget will continue to be matched by increased accountability and improved performance and asks them to expand the tools of partnership from aid to trade, transit and investment.",""]],"32":[[1,"8","2","Digital Strategy for Citizen Access to Information and Services","Align delivery of core state functions to the citizen-centric injunctions and values of the constitution, especially the equality of rights between men and women (A-SDG 5), relying on a digital strategy to enhance citizen access to information and services, thereby enhancing trust between the citizens and the state, and ensuring that Afghanistan citizens can enjoy prosperous and fulfilling lives.",""],[1,"15","3","Citizen-Centered Public Institutions and Organizations","With the foundation in place, the government and the people are committed to accelerating the momentum of building citizen-centered public institutions and organizations.",""],[1,"15","3","Governance Digitization Initiative","A major effort at digitization of governance is underway to connect the citizens more directly with the state and to eliminate uneven access to information on citizenship rights.",""],[1,"45","7","Chief Advisor on Digitization and Technology","the President has appointed a Chief Advisor on Digitization and Technology.",""],[1,"45","7","Mobile Money, Electronic ID, and E-Passport Deployment","Implementation of a mobile money payment system and issuance of electronic IDs and machine-readable passports to our citizens are among our top priorities for now.",""],[1,"45","7","Electronic Procurement Reform","moving to electronic procurement, will be significant.",""]],"33":[[1,"20","11","Civil Society Engagement for Community-Level NPP Delivery","Engage civil society organizations to ensure NPPs are delivered on the ground at the community level.",""],[1,"24","3","Citizen's Charter Rapid COVID-19 Relief Delivery","The government also plans to harness lessons from the success of the Citizen's Charter program for directing rapid COVID-19 relief to those most in need.",""],[1,"39","2","Citizen's Charter Program Expansion","We will further expand the Citizen's Charter program to support people who are vulnerable to structural risks and whose livelihoods are affected by the COVID-19 pandemic.",""],[1,"58","10","Community Development Council Infrastructure and Social Services Expansion","SO 7: Extend core infrastructure and social services to all communities through CDCs, and empower communities in urban and rural areas to set and achieve their own development goals and unleash their long-term growth potential.",""],[1,"60","6","Improved Service Delivery through Community Development Councils","IR 7.1: Reduce poverty and deepen the relationship between citizens and the state, by improved services delivery through CDCs.",""],[1,"60","6","Community Development Council Participation in Social Service Planning and Monitoring","IR 7.3: Encourage the active participation of CDCs in the design, implementation and monitoring of social services, such as health, education, and support to the local agriculture sector.",""],[1,"63","18","Community Outreach for Basic Infrastructure and Minimum Services","IO 7.1: The outreach of the charter extended to ### communities by 2025 to build basic infrastructure and deliver minimum standard health and education services (up from 10000 in 2019).",""]],"34":[[1,"9","4","National Budget Reform for Planning and Implementation","We reformed our national budget to become a more effective planning and implementation tool for the government's vision.",""],[1,"9","4","National Program Development Streamlining and Guidance","We have also worked with line ministries to streamline the national program development process and provided detailed guidance on upstream strategically fit, costing, results-orientation, implementation plans, procurement planning as well as sequencing of the investment pipelines both on and off-budget.","line ministries"],[1,"16","2","National Development Priorities and Reform Framework","This follow-up Framework presents a renewed narrative for our long-term development, based on the progress made and lessons learned over the past five years, and provides high-level guidance to government and other stakeholders.",""],[1,"16","2","Priority Reform Agenda","It defines our immediate and long-term development priorities, highlights key reforms needed moving forward, and outlines priority investments needed to achieve our development goals.",""],[1,"16","2","Fiscal Strategy for Budget Allocation and Public Investment Management","This context leads to a fiscal strategy that will guide budgetary allocations to support the policy goals laid out and ensure the sustainable management of the public investment.",""],[1,"19","4","National Budget Formulation and Performance Review Process","We will further strengthen the national budget formulation process as the primary tool for planning and implementing our development and security expenditures.",""],[1,"20","7","Public Investment Management and Budget Reform Integration","Be integrated into the ongoing public investment management and budget reforms and the alignment of functions and levels of government.",""],[1,"20","8","Off-Budget Funding Streamlining and Alignment","Streamline and align off-budget funding.",""],[1,"20","12","Reprioritization of Existing National Priority Programs","We are reprioritizing the existing national priority programs that have been developed and operationalized over the recent years to respond to emerging priorities in line with fiscal realities.",""],[1,"22","4","Outcome-Based Budget Reform","The national budget is the main implementation and planning tool for the government.",""],[1,"22","5","Reorganization of National Priority Programs","Second, we have reorganized our National Priority Programs to be more focused and have placed them within a more coherent framework of Peace Building, State Building, and Market Building.",""],[1,"22","6","Policy Implementation Framework for Strategic Choices","To ensure that our program is implemented well, we will use the framework of legitimacy, policy, and action to ensure that our strategy achieves public impact.",""],[1,"27","4","Investment Pipeline Development for Priority Sectors","Each prioritized sector will produce an investment pipeline aligned to this goal and in line with available resources",""],[1,"37","2","Budget and Public Financial Management Reform Strategy","Budget and PFM systems are being improved to address the challenges faced by the country and ensure the efficient use of the financial resources at its disposal.",""],[1,"37","2","Fiscal Space Creation and Priority Allocation","The government will aim to create fiscal space and allocate it to top priorities.",""],[1,"37","2","Anti-Corruption Public Finance Reform Strategy","A comprehensive reform strategy will examine public finances through an anti-corruption lens with the aim of improving tax collection through shifts from informal to formal collections, targeting tax arrears and clearing backlogs, broadening the tax base through improved enforcement, and streamlining management of customs facilities and ports to ease trade and improve efficiency in revenue generation.",""],[1,"37","2","Public Investment Management and Expenditure Efficiency Reform","The government will also seek to improve efficiency and savings in current expenditures by improving the public investment management process for project selection in the budget, conducting a portfolio review of the existing projects and programs in the budget, targeting anti-corruption measures to reduce misuse of public funds, and reviewing government institutions to improve operational and structural efficiency and address overlaps.",""],[1,"46","3","Budget Reform and Aid Alignment Framework","Afghanistan's reform agenda will further build on the budget reforms carried out over the past years to ensure that the budget is the primary instrument for carrying out the policy.",""],[1,"49","4","Measures to Strengthen Fiduciary Integrity and Trust in Government Financial Management Systems","To address the donor partners' concerns over the fiduciary integrity of our financial management systems, the following measures to build trust and credibility in government systems are proposed for 2020-21:",""],[1,"49","8","Supreme Audit Office Strengthening Reform","Strengthen the Supreme Audit office by fast-tracking the SAO law to ensure greater operational independence and invest in its capacity to carry out its required duties in the oversight of the budget;",""],[1,"51","3","Revenue Administration Reform and Taxpayer Segmentation","A wide range of reforms and restructuring has been implemented within the Afghanistan revenue department, including the segmentation of taxpayers into Large, Medium, and Small offices (LTO, MTO, STO) and the roll-out of these offices to regional provinces, the professionalization of the tax services - fast-track filing and e-forms - and implementation of Standard Integrated Government Tax Administration System (SIGTAS).",""],[1,"52","2","Tax Administration and Revenue Mobilization Reform","Increasing domestic revenue mobilization through improving tax administration, ramping up the pace to reforms, expanding the tax base, and finding new sources of revenue",""],[1,"52","2","Fiscal Expenditure, Debt, and Grant Management Improvement","Ensuring fiscal sustainability and macroeconomic stability by improved management of fiscal expenditure, debt, and international grants",""],[1,"52","4","Macroeconomic Stabilization","Progress will continue on macroeconomic stabilization to minimize the risk of shocks.",""],[1,"52","6","Increase Civilian Expenditures","The government will increase civilian expenditures in line with national priorities and population growth.",""],[1,"60","2","Revenue Collection and Fiscal Management Improvement","IR 5.2.1: improve revenue collection and fiscal management.",""],[1,"60","2","Expenditure Consolidation Measures","IR 5.2.2: Adopt expenditure consolidation measures.",""]],"35":[[1,"6","4","Import Substitution and Domestic Competitiveness Strategy","Import substitution, where the current import bill is seven times that of our exports, will automatically result in favorable changes of trade, as our products will compete both on quality and price with imported basic commodities.",""],[1,"9","1","Aid-to-Trade Partnership Expansion","Expand the tools of international partnership from aid to trade, transit, investment, guarantees, and digital networks of knowledge.",""],[1,"21","11","Trade and Transit Initiatives Support Programme","Support for trade and transit initiatives. Design and implement.",""],[1,"25","4","Export-Led Growth Strategy","the government under ANPDF-2 considers export-led growth as the thrust of its growth strategy",""],[1,"25","4","Trade and Transit Development Programme","trade, transit, and small-scale labor-intensive industrial development as its top national priority programs",""],[1,"26","4","Export-Led Growth Strategy","Export-led growth will remain the main thrust of our strategy of growth.",""],[1,"26","4","Import Substitution and Market-Building Review","However, given widespread protectionism, dumping and smuggling and lack of adherence to World Trade Organization rules that Afghanistan joined in the hope of having a level playing field in trade and transit, import substitution will be a complementary thrust.",""],[1,"26","8","Export Development and Import Substitution in Targeted Sectors","Promoting export development and import substitution in targeted sectors and economic activities where Afghanistan has a potential comparative advantage;",""]],"36":[[1,"42","1","Regional Trade Facilitation and Connectivity Investment","Afghanistan will continue to strengthen policy cooperation with the neighboring countries and invest in infrastructure to make trade flows with our neighbors faster and cheaper.",""],[1,"43","2","Export Corridor Development Initiative","This includes the establishment of Air Corridors to increase air freight exports, the creation of four rail links to increase rail exports, the establishment of the Lapis Lazuli route to increase road exports, and moving forward with the Chabahar Port to diversify our potential exports by sea.",""],[1,"50","2","Regional Economic Integration and Trade Route Expansion Policy","Fortunately, the government's active regional integration policy for economic cooperation enhanced Afghanistan's reach to wider international markets through multiple new trading routes, including Chabhar Port, the historical Lapiz Lazuli route, the Sino-Afghanistan Special Railway Transportation Project, and the Air corridors.",""],[1,"61","3","Border Logistics and Regulatory Improvement","IR 11.4: Increase the impacts through improvements in logistics and regulatory constraints at border points.",""],[1,"64","3","Investment in Key Customs Centers","Investing in eight key customs centers to expedite flows.",""]],"37":[[1,"60","7","Transport, Communications, and Internet Access Expansion","IR 9.2: Improve access to transportation, communication and internet for all citizens.",""],[1,"61","3","Internet Connectivity Expansion and Regional Fiber-Optic Links","IR 11.5: Create new economic opportunities by expanding internet connectivity, including regional fiber-optic cable connections.",""]],"38":[[1,"27","2","Labor Migration Agreement Negotiation and Implementation","Accelerating the process of negotiations and implementation of bilateral and multilateral agreements with neighboring, regional and trans-regional countries to sending and employing Afghan laborers abroad, which will help in lowering unemployment and increasing household revenue through remittances.",""],[1,"27","3","Job Creation Program Financing and Planning","Comprehensive planning and financing of job creation programs (the Eshiteghal Zaiee - Karmondena (EZ-Kar), PLACED, and technical and vocational programs to equip people with the high-demand skills and abilities):",""]],"39":[[1,"6","3","Rule of Law and Anti-Corruption Reform","we will establish the rule of law and continue to combat corruption, criminality, and violence.",""],[1,"8","4","Anti-Corruption Implementation and Enforcement Measures","Building on the legislative and institutional reforms of recent years, the government will focus on implementation and operations, including asset management, audits, and prosecutions to deliver visible results and increase citizen's trust in public institutions",""],[1,"35","4","Anti-Corruption Measures","The government of the Islamic Republic of Afghanistan considers corruption as an existential threat to Afghanistan peace and development and commits to:",""],[1,"35","5","Anti-Corruption Reform in Government Institutions","Reduce and remove the opportunities and incentives for corruption within government institutions.",""],[1,"35","6","Public Sector Governance and Accountability Reform","Create functional and accountable government institutions and ensure transparent and competitive processes in civil service recruitments, procurements, and budget execution.",""],[1,"35","7","Public Asset Management and Audit Strengthening","Ensure better management of assets and improved audit functions to create budget learning cycles.",""],[1,"35","8","Advanced Anti-Corruption Data Technology Measures","Encourage and mandate the use of advanced technologies to collect, analyze, and share data to detect and deter corrupt behavior.",""],[1,"35","9","Public Confidence Restoration in Justice Institutions and Civil Service","Restore and improve public confidence on justice institutions and civil service by advancing",""],[1,"36","2","Anti-Corruption Public Financial Management Reform","Improve and ensure effective Public Financial Management through an anti-corruption lens.",""],[1,"36","3","Security Sector Anti-Corruption Reform","End corruption in the security sector by developing strong anti-corruption security institutions and improving assets management.",""],[1,"36","4","Judicial Sector Reform and Anti-Corruption Enforcement","Continue reforms in the judicial sector and improve the judiciary's ability to investigate, prosecute, and punish the corrupt.",""],[1,"36","5","Anti-Corruption Operational Coordination Mechanism","Create stronger anti-corruption operational coordination by engaging the civil society and independent monitoring institutions.",""],[1,"36","6","Decentralized Anti-Corruption Oversight and Coordination","Decentralize anti-corruption initiatives from Kabul to provincial centers by increasing oversight and coordination at the sub-national level.",""],[1,"36","7","Regular High Council Oversight of Anti-Corruption and Rule of Law Tasks","the High Council on Rule of Law and Anti-Corruption will meet regularly to oversee the completion of the following critical tasks: completion of promised benchmarks; enforcement of decisions of the Attorney General's office by the police; finalization of an interim anti-corruption strategy; finalization of the anti-corruption plans of each of the NPPs; process mapping and of the judicial chain and organizational review of decision-rights and coordination by all the organs of the state on rule of law and corruption and reform of the rules and practices.",""],[1,"38","1","Anti-Corruption Institutional Reform and Enforcement Strengthening","To help prosecute the corrupt, the Afghan government is committed to increasing the efficiency of the law enforcement institutions (Major Crimes Task Force, Asset Recovery Directorate and Attorney General Deputy for Anti-Corruption), including setting standards, adopting tools to speed up the process and enhance coordination, capacity appraisal, and building, regular public reporting, transparency in court decisions, etc.","Major Crimes Task Force | Asset Recovery Directorate | Attorney General Deputy for Anti-Corruption"],[1,"38","1","Customs, Budget, and Treasury Anti-Corruption Reforms","Further reforms of customs, budget, and treasury are a vital area of anti-corruption reform.",""],[1,"38","1","Private Sector and Civil Society Anti-Bribery Engagement","We will continue to engage the private sector and civil society, including the media, to take part in fighting bribery and to bring transparency during the licensing period.",""],[1,"38","1","Consolidation of Preventive Anti-Corruption Bodies into the Anti-Corruption Commission","Finally, we will progressively merge many of the existing preventive anti-corruption bodies into the independent Anti-Corruption Commission to be fully compliant with UNCAC.",""],[1,"40","4","Corruption Risk Management Across Project Cycle","Manage the integrity and corruption threats at all stages of the process, from project conception to delivery.",""],[1,"49","5","National Accountability Strategy","Embark on a hard-hitting National Accountability Strategy that combines public finance reform with anti-corruption measures to achieve greater efficiency and accountability in public finance.",""],[1,"49","6","Anti-Corruption Commission Establishment and Operationalization","Create and operationalize the Anti-Corruption Commission (ACC)",""],[1,"49","7","Asset Declaration Verification for Public Officials","Verify asset declarations starting with law enforcement, customs, and tax administration officials.",""],[1,"60","1","Anti-Corruption Efforts","IR 5.1.1: Enhance momentum on anti-corruption efforts.",""],[1,"60","3","Anti-Corruption Public Finance Reform Strategy","Continue to implement a comprehensive reform strategy to examine government finances through an anti-corruption lens.",""],[1,"63","6","Interim Anti-Corruption Strategy Finalization","The interim anti-corruption strategy and the anti-corruption plans of each of the NPPs are about to finalize.",""]],"40":[[1,"36","8","Subnational Governance Reform and Review","There is a need to evaluate the strengths and weaknesses of current subnational structures, review, and revisit sub-national legal frameworks.",""],[1,"36","8","Inclusive Subnational Planning and Service Delivery","A strong state presence with inclusive planning, budgeting, and spending,, and the provision of services, including administrative, infrastructure, security, and legal protection, are essential.",""],[1,"36","8","Legal and Structural State Reform","Changes needed will require both legal and structural reforms.",""],[1,"36","9","District Administration Strengthening and Vertical Governance Alignment","Strengthening of district administration and aligning it with the village and municipality and province ... is among the top priorities of the government.",""],[1,"36","10","Economic Zone Establishment and Regional Development Authority Coordination","The government commits to establishing 8 economic zones corresponding to the seven military and police corps plus the economic zone of the capital.",""],[1,"37","1","Regional Development Authorities Establishment","The regional development authorities (RDAs) will be established as State-Owned Corporation (SOC), each responsible for the designing, planning, implementation, and monitoring of development projects in their respective regions.",""],[1,"37","1","Local Councils and District and Municipality Elections","Also, we will establish local councils and conduct the district and municipality councils' elections to improve local governance and enhance people's role in government and decision-making.",""],[1,"37","1","Governor Participation in Cabinet Sessions","the government endorsed the digital inclusion of governors in cabinet sessions where each cabinet meeting gives a slot to a governor to speak on behalf of others.",""],[1,"60","1","Regional Development Authorities Establishment","IR 5.1.3: Improve sub-national governance by establishing Regional Development Authorities responsible for designing, planning, implementing and monitoring of development projects.",""]],"41":[[1,"3","23","Women's Economic Empowerment Program","4.9.5 A Re-focused Women's Economic Empowerment Program (WEE-NPP) (2017",""],[1,"11","3","Civil Society Engagement on Women's Participation","The government will continue to engage civil society organizations, particularly organizations representing women, to assess and respond to such challenges at all levels.",""],[1,"11","3","Women's Capacity Building and Enabling Environment under NPPs","The government initiatives under NPPs are building the women's capacity and ensuring an enabling environment to allow them to improve their livelihood.",""],[1,"27","4","Women’s Economic Participation and Girls’ Education Promotion","encourage more women to work in the education, health care, and other sectors where they are underrepresented, promote girls' enrollment in education, and create systems to reduce gender- based violence",""],[1,"27","4","Women’s Participation in Market Building","We also invest on promoting the role and participation of women in our market building process",""],[1,"44","2","Women's Economic Empowerment National Priority Program","We must bolster coordination, implementation, and results in a re-focused and re-invigorated WEE-NPP over the next five years.",""],[1,"61","11","Women's Labor Market Participation and Equal Opportunity Support","IR 15.1: Enable women to join the local, regional, and national labor markets, and compete on an equal footing in various social, political and economic affairs in the country.",""],[1,"61","11","Women's Start-up Technical and Financial Access Support","IR 15.2: Improve women's access to start-up technical and financial resources.",""]],"42":[[1,"30","7","Inclusive Peace Negotiation and Consensus-Building Process","Our strategy is to ensure every Afghan has a stake in the peace discussions.",""],[1,"30","7","Peace Process Coordination and Dialogue Support","Peace is our foremost priority and requires programs to coordinate talks, a strong security sector to push the other side to the peace table, and the provision of justice.",""],[1,"31","1","National Dialogue for Conflict Resolution and Shared Vision","a national dialogue from the village to the national level to focus on healing and owning a common vision of the future, reinforcing the commitment to resolve conflicts through legal and political means",""],[1,"31","3","Peace Process Engagement Framework","This will initially include laying the groundwork for building trust among the parties.",""],[1,"31","3","Sustained Taliban Engagement Capacity","It will also create capabilities to engage with the Taliban on a sustained basis.",""],[1,"31","3","Afghan Peace Process Support Programme","The Peace NPP aims to promote the prospects for a negotiated settlement to Afghan war by fostering the Afghan peace process, continuing efforts to reintegrate lower-level fighters, enticing insurgents away from the battlefield, improving institutional capacity to support the peace process, and providing jobs, security and service to people.",""],[1,"31","4","Inclusive Peace Process Consultation Mechanism","The government of Afghanistan will continue to approach the consultative Loya Jirga, elected representatives of the people, and the civil society organizations in order to link the grassroots with the national processes as we go ahead with the intra-Afghan peace negotiations.",""],[1,"59","7","Unconditional Peace Negotiation and Political Recognition for the Taliban","Offer an unconditional peace negotiation to Taliban and recognize the group as a political party.",""],[1,"59","9","Peace Consensus-Building Initiative","Continue attempts to build a national, regional and international consensus to bring peace in Afghanistan.",""]],"43":[[1,"32","1","Sustained Investment in Armed Forces Capabilities","This requires sustained investment in our armed forces and in particular, our special forces, air force, and intelligence capabilities.",""],[1,"32","1","Training, Logistics, and Medical Support for Security Forces","We will also invest in better training, logistics capabilities, and medical capabilities for our forces.",""],[1,"32","1","Organizational and Expenditure Review of Defense and Interior Ministries","A comprehensive organizational and expenditure review of the Ministries of Defense and Interior is underway to ensure the affordability and sustainability of our forces.","Ministries of Defense and Interior"],[1,"32","1","Continued Security Sector Fund Support","Continued support from LOTFA for the police and C-STCA and other funds for the army will be essential to the success of these reforms.",""],[1,"59","15","Security Sector Institutional Capacity Enhancement","IR 2.2: Enhance the capacity of the security sector institutions to prevent violence, terrorism and crime.",""]],"44":[[1,"32","2","Accelerated Police, Justice Ministry, and Prison System Reform","However, the police and the Ministry of Justice still need accelerated reforms, as so does the prison system.","Ministry of Justice"],[1,"33","4","Law Enforcement Reform Continuation","The government is committed to the continuation of the initiated reforms in the ministry of interior affairs and other line organizations.","ministry of interior affairs"],[1,"33","4","Police Professionalization and Oversight Improvement","Better law enforcement requires developing efficient policing, promoting transparency, oversight, personal training, and encouraging the use of technology.",""],[1,"33","4","Judicial Authority Strengthening for Law Enforcement","In cooperation with TAAC - North, we work toward more professionalism in the police, ensure entrusting sufficient constitutional authority to judges, including the interim power to seize assets, etc. for effective law enforcement.",""]],"45":[[1,"32","3","Justice Sector Access and Legal Awareness Measures","To protect rights, punish perpetrators of human rights violations and facilitate wider access to fair and viable justice, the government adopts the following measures.",""],[1,"33","1","Legal Awareness and Justice Access Campaigns","Enhancing public knowledge of the justice system through legal awareness campaigns including legal aid centers, provision of information about the justice system through media, the civil society at the grassroots level, and trained employed people/volunteers to serve as advocates and providers of legal advice, and primary and secondary-level educational curricula.",""],[1,"34","2","Justice Sector Strengthening Program","We renew our commitment to continue to strengthen the justice and judicial sector.",""],[1,"59","17","Judicial Independence Reform","IR 3.2: Ensure the independence of the judiciary.",""],[1,"59","18","Expansion of Formal Justice Institutions Nationwide","IR 3.3: Extend the reach of the formal institutions of justice throughout the country.",""],[1,"59","19","Legal Awareness Campaigns for Justice Institutions","IR 3.4: Enhance people's confidence on institutions of justice by reducing misunderstandings about the formal justice administration through legal awareness campaigns.",""]],"46":[[1,"38","2","Food Security Improvement Commitment","We reaffirms our commitment to improve food security and progressing towards A-SDG 2 on zero hunger.",""],[1,"38","2","Human Capital Program Reprioritization","The overall human capital program will be reprioritized to further strengthen further the quality and access to education, health, and social protection programs that build and sustain productive human capital in Afghanistan, with the aim of driving economic growth and alleviating poverty.",""],[1,"38","3","Operationalization of Human Capital NPP Pillars","The pillars of the HC-NPP are being operationalized through the National Health strategy, National education strategic Plan - which is now being updated to cover the entire period up to 2030, the Higher education development Project, and the National technical and vocational education and training (TVET) strategy 2020 -2024.",""]],"47":[[1,"46","2","Aid Effectiveness and Donor Coordination Framework","We will continue sectoral discussions launched in 2019 piloting in education, health, agriculture, justice, and subnational governance with donor partners to coordinate efforts.",""],[1,"46","3","On-budget Donor Financing Channeling","Channeling donor funds through the national budget is not only a more efficient, cost-effective use of money than off-budget programming, it also underscores that supporting the Afghan budget process is a necessary step towards a successful donor exit strategy.",""],[1,"46","3","Government Systems-Based Aid Management","Using government systems not only reduces unit costs but is an essential pre-condition for the government to take full responsibility for performance.",""],[1,"47","1","Donor Portfolio Alignment and Aid Effectiveness Reviews","We intend to continue this practice to align donor portfolios to government priorities, ensure value for money, and implement basic aid effectiveness principles.",""],[1,"47","1","Expanded Use of Country Systems for Aid Disbursement","As the government continues to strengthen its Public Financial Management systems, we also expect our donor partners to make increased use of country systems to disburse aid.",""],[1,"48","3","Policy-Based Conditionality for On-Budget Support","We, therefore, propose that our partners work with us on a set of policy conditions in return for on-budget support to enable us to focus national energies on building systems and programs, and cultivating leaderships and management skills, in the government and the private sector.",""],[1,"48","7","Predictable Pooled Aid for National Budget Support","Commit to predictable pooled aid to support the national budget.",""],[1,"48","9","Conditional Aid Enhancement for Reform Implementation and Budget Priorities","Enhance levels of conditional aid to strengthen reform implementation and provide discretionary funds to finance national budget priorities.",""],[1,"48","11","Regular Aid Portfolio Review Mechanism","Work with the Ministry of Finance on regular aid portfolio reviews to ensure the alignment","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"52","2","International Grant Financing for Government Activities and Priority Programs","International grants to Afghanistan will remain crucial for ensuring continued government activities, financing the national budget and national priority programs",""]],"49":[[1,"19","4","National Development Policy Coordination and Planning Framework","The method for planning and implementing development policies will continue as laid out in the first ANPDF.",""],[1,"19","4","Ministerial Policy, Programme, and Project Implementation","Each minister is responsible for implementing policies, programs, and projects related to his/her ministry.",""],[1,"20","9","Inter-Ministerial Coordination with National Priority Programmes","Be aligned and coordinated with other NPPs to maximize effect and provide a platform for inter-ministerial cooperation and coordination.",""]],"50":[[1,"7","2","National Defense and Security Capability Strengthening","To preserve the stability of the country, we must maintain and enhance the capabilities of our national defense and security forces.",""]],"51":[[1,"7","3","Inclusive and Participatory Peace Process Mechanisms","The government of the Islamic Republic of Afghanistan will make sure that the peace process is participatory and inclusive of all segments of Afghan society, particularly women, youth, minorities, differently-abled persons and families of Martyrs, Afghan diaspora, Kuchis, civil society, and the private sector, through convening the consultative Loya Jirgas at the national level and other such mechanisms at provincial, district and village levels.",""]],"52":[[1,"14","1","Nationally Determined Contribution for Greenhouse Gas Emissions Reduction","developing the first Nationally Determined Contribution that pledges a reduction of 13.6 percent in GHG emissions upon the availability of an estimated US$ 17.4 billion.",""]],"53":[[1,"18","3","Inclusive Supply Chain Coordination for Essential Goods","Close coordination between the government, the private sector, communities, the Ulama and civil society has been essential to the functioning of the supply chains of essential goods.",""]],"54":[[1,"5","2","Expand Investments in Health, Education, Humanitarian Development, and Wellbeing","Afghanistan will be able to expand investments in the health, education, humanitarian development and wellbeing of our people",""],[1,"8","5","COVID-19 Relief and Recovery Program","We will deal with the adverse effects of COVID-19 by refocusing existing programs on relief, with a special focus on the poor and ultra-poor communities and female-headed households - and implement a stimulus program to usher a sustained recovery.",""],[1,"19","2","COVID-19 Relief and Recovery Response","In the short-run, COVID-19 relief and recovery is the government's most urgent priority.",""],[1,"19","2","Emergency Resource Mobilization for Immediate Needs","We are restructuring existing programs, closing non-performing projects, and using all available resources, both on and off-budget, to help meet the immediate needs of the Afghan people.",""],[1,"21","2","COVID-19 and Long-Term Response Program","New COVID19 & long-term Response. Design and implement program",""],[1,"21","10","Reprogramming of Public Health Projects for COVID-19 Response","Reprogramming of Sehatmandi and other public health projects to deal with healthcare issues during and after COVID_19.",""],[1,"22","5","COVID-19 Response Program","In the short-term, we must focus on our COVID-19 response program to ensure that our citizens remain safe, that food is provided during the crisis, and that we lay the groundwork for longer-term growth.",""],[1,"23","3","COVID-19 Response Short-Term Programs","In the near-term, the government plans to restructure existing resources into short-term programs for the COVID-19 response.",""],[1,"23","3","Development Partner Support for Pandemic Impact Mitigation","We have invited our development partners to assist in mitigating the impacts of the pandemic and we are working with them to review the current portfolio and redirect programs and funds towards addressing this new challenge.",""],[1,"24","2","COVID-19 Household Income Support Program","The government is establishing the National Meal Program to provide all Afghan households with income support for roughly two months.",""],[1,"24","6","Revised National Health Program","A revised National Health program, composed of three components focusing on Covid-19, expanding the scope and scale of the Sihat program, and a hospital reform and expansion effort.",""],[1,"24","12","Bread Distribution Program","Bread distribution program to meet the needs of those facing food shortages during the lockdown.",""]],"55":[[1,"19","2","Restructuring of Existing Programs","We are restructuring existing programs, closing non-performing projects, and using all available resources, both on and off-budget, to help meet the immediate needs of the Afghan people.",""],[1,"23","2","Fiscal Resource Reallocation and Project Prioritization","We plan to free up fiscal resources and expedite critical projects while canceling those that are lower performing.",""],[1,"23","2","Plan Revision and Priority Realignment","We are also realigning our priorities to be able to address the needs and the expectation of Afghans.",""],[1,"23","3","Resource Reprioritization and Implementation Mechanism Review","Moving forward, we are reprioritizing resource allocation and exploring new or revised mechanisms of implementation.",""],[1,"23","4","Growth Strategy Investment Pipeline Re-prioritization","We will re-prioritize the investment pipeline of the growth strategy considering alignment with COVID-19 response, recovery objectives and fiscal realities.",""],[1,"24","4","Reform and Revitalization of Existing National Priority Programmes","Our national objectives of the provision of healthcare and human security during the prevalence of COVID-19 and the goals of relief and recovery through a package of incentives for the market and the private sector will be realized through reform and revitalization of existing NPPs.",""]],"56":[[1,"26","1","Agriculture and Social Protection Coherence Measures","Efforts to increase agricultural yield and productivity should be complemented with social safety nets - promoting coherence between agriculture and social protection, boosting social policies, improving the resilience of farmers against natural hazards, and strengthening the capacity of producer organizations - to ensure household's sustainable income and food security.",""]],"57":[[1,"26","2","Private Sector Minimum Wage Law","A minimum wage law for the private sector",""],[1,"26","2","Public Sector Salary Gap Reduction Guideline","a comprehensive guideline for reducing the salary gap in public sector employment",""]],"58":[[1,"27","5","National Population Strategy Development","We will develop a national population strategy and devise necessary measures to address the challenge of rapid population growth.",""],[1,"27","5","Public Awareness Campaign on Family Size and Child Well-Being","We will engage civil society, Uluma, and organizations involved in protecting and promoting the rights of women and children to create public awareness about the consequences of having too many children.",""],[1,"27","5","Women's Empowerment for Household Decision-Making","We will continue to invest in empowering women to have a decision making power in the household in matters concerning them like child birth.",""],[1,"27","5","Population Growth Mainstreaming in Sector Policies and Priority Programs","The line ministries are already advised to include the parameter of population growth in their relevant policies and priority programs in",""]],"59":[[1,"29","4","National Adaptation Plan Finalization","Afghanistan is finalizing its National Adaptation Plan (NAP) as well as the National Climate Change Strategy Action Plan (ACCSAP).",""],[1,"29","4","Climate Change Strategy Action Plan Finalization","Afghanistan is finalizing its National Adaptation Plan (NAP) as well as the National Climate Change Strategy Action Plan (ACCSAP).",""],[1,"29","4","Low Emission Development Strategy Development and Implementation","Through these plans and the Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC) processes, our overall vision is to enhance the adaptive capacity and resilience of Afghanistan's agriculture, environment, and population to climate change, while developing and implementing Low Emission Development Strategies (LEDS).",""],[1,"29","6","Sector Environmental Impact Reduction Action Plans","To enhance sustainable development in these sectors, the GoIRA pledges to reduce the impacts of all sectors on the environment by developing and implementing required action plans.",""],[1,"29","8","National Environmental and Climate Change Funds","The establishment of national environmental and climate change funds that can combine public and private finance flows that would allow engagement across sectors to unlock high",""]],"60":[[1,"30","1","Environmental Investment Financing Package","This would comprise a range of financing tools, including loans, equity, guarantees and grants.",""],[1,"30","2","Public and Private Sector Capacity Development for NEP Implementation","Capacity development in the public and private sectors that would support the implementation of initiatives under the NEP priority areas.",""],[1,"30","3","Research and Development Scale-Up for Environmental Solutions","The scaling up of research and development that would provide up-to-date, evidence-based solutions for Afghanistan's environmental challenges.",""]],"61":[[1,"30","4","Women's Training and Access to Renewable Energy Programme","The government will provide training and facilitate wider access to renewable sources of energy.",""],[1,"30","5","Women’s Recycling Industry Capacity Building Support","The government commits to offer capacity building training for professional development and supportive tools.",""]],"62":[[1,"30","8","Post-Peace Reintegration and Resettlement Measures","At least six critical tasks will have to be dealt with to make peace sustainable.",""],[1,"34","3","Former Fighters and Returning Citizens Reintegration Plan","We will develop a reintegration plan for former fighters that does more than provide a cash stipend and food during the first phase.",""],[1,"34","3","Ongoing Support for Former Fighters Reintegration","We must stay engaged with such former fighters to ensure they have an incentive to remain with civil society.",""],[1,"34","3","Regional Reintegration Framework with Neighboring States","Second, we must engage with our neighboring states to create a framework for the successful reintegration of our citizens.",""],[1,"34","4","Returnee and IDP Reintegration Support Framework","A recently signed Presidential decree 305 and the corresponding guidelines lay the foundations for the effective reintegration of returnees and IDPs.",""],[1,"34","6","Orderly and Safe Migration Policy","promoting orderly and safe migration is one of the government's priority policy areas enshrined in the (A-SDG 10.7).",""],[1,"34","6","Skills Enhancement and Managed Migration Support","We promote sustainable economic growth, job creation, and poverty reduction in combination with support for skills enhancement and managed migration as essential interventions for reducing large-scale irregular migration.",""],[1,"34","6","Regional Migration Cooperation Framework","it requires a regional approach involving the regional actors - Iran, Pakistan, Turkey, and international humanitarian organizations such as UNHCR, and IOM.",""],[1,"35","1","Regional Migration Negotiation and Afghan Refugee Support Arrangements","We need to negotiate the necessary legal and administrative arrangements in a regional setup together with additional economic incentives for reducing illegal migration and also finding effective solutions to the manifold challenges that the Afghan refugees are facing in Pakistan and Iran, including but not limited to humanitarian and security challenges.",""],[1,"62","3","Combatant Reintegration Programme","IO 1.2.5: Integrate ## combatants by 2025.",""]],"63":[[1,"33","2","Integration of Informal Justice Mechanisms into the Formal Justice Sector","Therefore, we need to analyze in consultation with the religious scholars, civil society, lawyers, and experts the compatibility of informal justice models with the national and international standards on human rights and, to the extent possible, integrate them within the formal justice sector.",""],[1,"33","2","Development of Rights-Compatible Religious and Cultural Justice Alternatives","In areas that the religious and traditional mechanisms of justice provision are in contradiction with the human rights conventions, the attempt would be made to limit their application and/or develop religiously and culturally alternatives to such mechanisms.",""],[1,"33","3","Transitional Justice Mechanisms","After the consolidation of a peace deal, the government of Afghanistan will also work toward establishing required mechanisms such 'truth and reconciliation commissions,' 'special tribunals,' 'reparations programs' etc. to address alleged past war crimes, serious human rights violation and crimes against humanity.",""],[1,"33","3","Transitional Justice Provisions in Peace Agreement","The peace negotiators of the government of the Islamic Republic of Afghanistan would advocate for the inclusion of the provisions for transitional justice in a peace deal with the Taliban and the government will stand by it after the peace is established.",""],[1,"59","11","Local Dispute Mitigation through Property Rights Implementation","Mitigate the local level disputes by defining and ensuring effective implementation of property rights.",""],[1,"62","1","Local-Level Property Rights Dispute Resolution Mechanisms","IO 1.2.3: ## local-level dispute resolution mechanisms of property rights enforcement established.",""]],"64":[[1,"33","5","Intensive Training on International and Humanitarian Law","Intensive training, specifically focusing on",""],[1,"34","1","Afghan Civilian Mitigation Team","the Afghan Civilian Mitigation Team is established which is responsible for tracking, analyzing, and mitigating civilian harms and investigating civilian casualties timely and transparently.",""]],"65":[[1,"39","3","Infrastructure Project Preparation and Resettlement Planning","For example, properly detailed designs, acquisition of land, and resettlement plans for road construction projects are required in advance of the implementation of infrastructure projects.",""],[1,"39","4","Infrastructure Development Program","The infrastructure development program with transport, energy and digital connectivity at its core, is focused on investments to improve access to services, inputs and markets to Afghans at the local level, across the country, and regionally.",""],[1,"40","1","Infrastructure Development Project Portfolio","The infrastructure development NPP outlines the core strategies to improve infrastructures by orchestrating comprehensive and effective short-term, medium- term and long-term projects for the development of transportation (roads, highways, and railways), energy and ICT infrastructures.",""],[1,"40","2","Adoption of OECD Infrastructure Governance Recommendations","We are committed to adopting and implement the OECD's nine recommendations for getting infrastructure governance right.",""],[1,"40","3","National Long-Term Strategic Vision for Infrastructure Services","Establish a national long-term strategic vision that addresses infrastructure service needs.",""],[1,"40","5","Delivery Mode Selection Criteria Framework","Establish clear criteria to guide the choice of delivery mode (PPP vs. direct public provision, etc.).",""],[1,"40","8","Early Stakeholder Consultation Process","Integrate a consultation process early enough so that decisions benefit from real stakeholder engagement.",""],[1,"40","9","Infrastructure Policy Coordination Across Levels of Government","Co-ordinate infrastructure policy across levels of government in such a way that investment decisions by central and subnational governments are coherent.",""],[1,"40","10","Cost-Benefit Analysis for Affordability and Value for Money","Guard affordability and value for money by using and applying cost-benefit and other methods rigorously and consistently.",""],[1,"40","12","Asset Lifecycle Performance Evaluation Mechanism","Integrate mechanisms to evaluate the performance of assets throughout their lifecycle.",""],[1,"58","12","Targeted Infrastructure Investment for Economic Activity and Exports","SO 9: Develop sustainable and resilient infrastructures to improve economic activities and boost exports and revenues through targeted investments on energy, minerals, transportation, communication, and regional integration projects.",""],[1,"60","7","Infrastructure Pipeline Planning and Delivery Reform","IR 9.3: Improve planning, implementation and delivery of the infrastructure pipeline, policy, and regulatory reforms.",""],[1,"61","2","Expedited Delivery of Major Planned Infrastructure Projects","IR 11.3: Proceed to expedited timelines with major planned projects, including TAPI, TAP, CASA-1000, and additional major transport infrastructure projects.",""]],"66":[[1,"40","11","Data Generation, Analysis, and Disclosure for Transparency and Accountability","Generate, analyze, and disclose useful data to increase transparency and ensure accountability.",""],[1,"46","4","Early Budget Recording of Off-Budget Support","financial information should be recorded on the budget as early as possible using standard budget categories to show the real picture of how resources are allocated across sectors and geography.",""],[1,"48","8","Financing Alignment Dialogue and Review Procedures","Improve dialogue and review procedures to ensure alignment of all financing with government priorities and quality of preparation.",""],[1,"48","10","Off-Budget Aid Flow Reporting Improvement","Improve reporting on off-budget aid flows to provide the Ministry of Finance with a comprehensive overall picture of public resource flows.","Ministry of Finance"],[1,"60","7","Infrastructure Fiscal Transparency and Accountability Mechanism","IR 9.4: Ensure transparency and accountability in utilization of the fiscal resources allocated to infrastructure development.",""]],"67":[[1,"61","2","Targeted Energy, Mineral, and Regional Integration Investment","IR 11.2: Accelerate targeted energy, mineral and regional integration investment to boost exports that will yield near-term benefits in terms of revenues.",""]],"68":[[1,"45","1","Criminalization of Illicit Natural Resource Exploitation","Adopting preventive measures such as the criminalization of the illicit exploitation of natural resources and ensuring the government's control of all mines and minerals across the country.",""],[1,"45","1","Government Control of Mines and Minerals","Adopting preventive measures such as the criminalization of the illicit exploitation of natural resources and ensuring the government's control of all mines and minerals across the country.",""],[1,"45","5","Natural Resources Governance Reform and Capacity Building","Improving national legislations and regulations and building capacity for the effective national management of natural resources.",""],[1,"59","20","Public Land Protection Against Usurpation and Illegal Use","IR 3.5: Prevent usurpation and illegal use of public land.",""]],"69":[[1,"46","4","Direct Donor Financing Support for Civil Society, Media, and Vulnerable Groups","We will continue to value and advance their role in our national development and support direct donor financing for human rights workers, press and media development, targeted programs for vulnerable groups, strategic private sector development initiatives and other activities critical for national development.",""]],"70":[[1,"47","4","National Tree Planting Program","we would like to be part of the 1 trillion trees initiative of the United States and environmental support programs of our other partners to announce and implement a program of 1 to 2 billion trees in the next four years.",""]]}});